    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XALTqTWCb7mgCXkNn1TRLx)_\n\nBack to the drawing board for `sp-thesis-dump`.\n\n- Deleted `libraries/modules/custom/sp-thesis-dump.el`.\n- Removed `sp-thesis-dump-trust-local-variables` (#201) from the doc; it went with the file. Your edit to the file on main (default `t`) is gone with it.\n- Every source block in `docs/tangles/custom/sp-thesis-dump.org` has `:tangle no`, and so do both `#+PROPERTY` lines, so a tangle cannot recreate the file. The doc says so in its intro.\n- Removed the module from `sp-late-modules` in `init.el` (it would fail to load), and updated `README.org` and `docs/architecture/load-order.org`.\n- Left `docs/architecture/skills/thesis-brain-dump/SKILL.md` in place, just no longer tangled.\n- CHANGELOG entry added.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container). Tangle check should pass: no tangled `sp-thesis-dump.el` is left to differ.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCPjeGYLGwpABH9DYo)_",
